dibly appropriate homage to the  famous Addams Family theme song  Nevermore Academy was founded in 1791.  its sole Mission has been to celebrate  and nurture those who lie on the fringes  of society principal Weems Ponders an  interesting question in the trailer in a  world full of normies  do you feel like an outcast she adds  that she too has felt like an oddity and  invites the audience to learn more about  the academy and all that is in store  through a special video presentation the  academy offers a wide range of studies  including werewolf reproduction and  Gorgon Anatomy that's only the beginning  of the experience for the students that  pass the application process  extracurricular activities run the gamut  from painting to archery the academy  also boasts such notable alumni as  Gothic novelist Edgar Allan Poe and  ignacius it as well as Morticia and  Gomez Adams in the words of two of the  students The well-respected Institute is  open to students from all walks of life  and death  in a featurette released on August 24th  Ortega opens up about her strenuous  schedule preparing to play the show's  titular character worried about stepping  into the role's Legacy she took fencing  and cello lessons twice a week her  commitment extended into every facet of  the work including nailing down  Wednesday's physicality I would walk  like Wednesday and I think that people  thought I might have been kind of crazy  because I wanted her to be specific  certain and assertive director Tim  Burton even compared Ortega's approach  to that of a silent movie actress  because of her ability to convey her  thoughts without words he praised her  performance saying that he couldn't  imagine anyone else in the role while  previous iterations of the character  were cartoony in Burton's estimation a  sense of reality was brought to the  story to give Wednesday even more  grounded character elements Ortega also  notes that this Wednesday is much more  socially awkward than previous 